I would argue that the Lily scooter stuff and how it kind of informs Lily's feeling of cold feet that she's developing about her wedding, it's kind of the deepest, most important part of this episode.
我认为莉莉和斯库特的剧情，以及它如何展现莉莉对即将到来的婚礼产生临阵退缩的情绪，可以说是这一集中最深刻、最重要的一部分。

00:28:58.660 --> 00:28:59.819
This episode's kind of like a fun one.
这一集其实挺有趣的。

00:28:59.819 --> 00:29:02.700
They need these late 20s something to try to sneak into a high school prom.
他们需要这群快三十岁的人去尝试潜入高中舞会。

00:29:02.700 --> 00:29:04.339
It's a fun, it's a fun bit.
这是一个很有趣的桥段。

00:29:04.339 --> 00:29:08.821
kind of, you know, it's like a lighter episode, but there's this heavy undercurrent.
你知道的，这算是一集比较轻松的节目，但其中暗藏着一股沉重的潜流。

00:29:08.821 --> 00:29:25.411
It's actually really interesting, you know, based on Lilly having felt suffocated by being too, in too serious of relationship in high school, deciding she wants to get to college and not do that and just be a little bit freer, a little bit like, you know, let's ease into being fully adult and fully committed.
其实真的很有趣，莉莉在高中时因为处于一段过于认真的感情中而感到窒息，于是决定上大学后不再那样，想更自由一点，稍微……你知道的，让我们慢慢过渡到完全成年和完全承担责任的状态。

00:29:25.411 --> 00:29:33.146
And then of course, you know, day one at Wesley and she meets Marshall, which is this wonderful scene of seeing that in college and that me cute.
然后当然，在卫斯理大学的第一天，她遇到了马歇尔，那是大学里的一场美妙的相遇，也是那场浪漫邂逅。

00:29:33.146 --> 00:29:38.321
I love how sweet that scene is, but also that it does play with the slate discordant note, right?
我喜欢那个场景有多甜蜜，但同时它也带有一点点不和谐的音符，对吧？

00:29:38.321 --> 00:29:59.712
Because it's sort of, it's very sweet to see and it's also planting this little time bomb that's going to go off later in the season and a few episodes at the end of the season of Marshall and Lily running into some problems and Lily wondering if things are moving a little too fast in her life and if she's kind of breaking a promise that, you know, 17, 18 year old her made to herself by doing that.
因为看到这一幕非常温馨，它同时也埋下了一个定时炸弹，这个炸弹将在本季后期以及本季末的几集中引爆，讲述马歇尔和莉莉遇到了一些问题，莉莉开始怀疑自己的生活是不是进展得太快了，这样做是否违背了当年十七八岁的自己对自己的承诺。

00:29:59.712 --> 00:30:01.579
And that's the deeper part of this.
而这才是这一集更深刻的部分。

00:30:01.579 --> 00:30:13.140
And this old man, he musted me, fell in love with you, knew who you're sitting, and now commercials.
还有这位老人，他肯定我，爱上了你，知道你坐在哪里，现在是广告时间。

00:30:13.140 --> 00:30:17.619
Hey, I'm Carl Radke.
嘿，我是卡尔·拉德克（Carl Radke）。

00:30:17.619 --> 00:30:26.099
You might know me from Bravo's Summer House, but on my podcast More Life, I get your favorite reality stars off the clock and into the conversations you don't usually get to hear.
你可能从 Bravo 电视台的《夏日山庄》（Summer House）中认识我，但在我的播客《更多生活》（More Life）中，我把你们最喜欢的真人秀明星带离工作状态，进入那些你们平时听不到的对话中。

00:30:26.099 --> 00:30:29.500
The deep stuff, the vulnerable stuff, the uncomfortable stuff.
那些深刻的内容、脆弱的内容、让人感到不自在的内容。

